    "reference": "Previous correctly mapped Armagon atlas is edit target; owner enhanced Shambler supplies permitted menacing redesign direction; original native Armagon fixes part correspondence.",
    "ownerDirection": "Take more liberties with boss visual design to make it menacing, guided by the difference between the original and enhanced Shambler.",
    "prompt": "Edit Image 1 into a significantly more MENACING, photorealistic Armagon boss production skin atlas. The owner explicitly wants creative liberties comparable to their enhanced Shambler, not just finer surface detail.\n\nINPUT ROLES:\nImage 1 is the EDIT TARGET and exact atlas layout. Image 2 is the owner's enhanced Shambler: use its dark tooth-filled facial focal point, weighty anatomical forms and convincing flesh quality as artistic direction, never copy its body or upright layout. Image 3 is the original Armagon skin, only a check on part correspondence and broad colour families.\n\nABSOLUTE MODEL FIT: preserve Image 1's complete 1323:1189 framing and normalized UV-island silhouettes/positions. Both Armagon halves remain SIDEWAYS, front on LEFT, back on RIGHT. The head of each sideways torso points toward the LEFT; the waist points toward the RIGHT. Cannons remain at the top and bottom of each half. Do not turn this into an upright character sheet. Keep all four detached orange-yellow flame islands exactly positioned and separate. Pure black unused background. No labels or text.\n\nREDESIGN THE CHARACTER:\nThe face in the LEFT/front half, around 15% of total image width and 48% of height, is currently a small mild brass grille. Turn this exact area into a vicious biomechanical skull-mask: a deep black/burgundy jaw cavity, irregular large ivory fangs and ossified ridges, a heavy crushed brow and thick scarred jaw tissue. Retain a smaller dark mechanical breathing core recessed within the face so it remains Armagon. Face anatomy must follow the sideways atlas: crown to LEFT, chin toward the RIGHT waist. Make this the clear threatening focal point. Do not put a second face on the back, torso, arms or guns.\n\nRebuild the organic surfaces into broad, heavy slabs of scarred muscle, taut tendons and knotted ash-tan hide, with stronger purposeful folds and deep anatomical recesses. Flesh should look powerful and fused into the cannon roots. Concentrate the existing burgundy wounded tissue at face and weapon interfaces; keep quieter areas of pale hide so the design reads at game distance. Use the Shambler's controlled sculptural forms. Avoid the current uniform glossy speckles, all-over cellular grain, gravel texture and candy-pink sheen.\n\nKeep the original-shaped massive cannon housings in dark charcoal/brown iron. Strengthen broad plate surfaces, recesses, bolts and scorched muzzle interiors, with selective worn edges and flesh-fused sockets. The back should have imposing vertebral and industrial cable structure, not a duplicated front face.\n\nPreserve recognizable Armagon pale flesh, dark earthy machinery, deep red wounds and orange flames, with bold internal anatomical redesign. No new horns, spikes or appendages outside existing silhouettes, no added eyes on unrelated parts, no decorative gold or neon, no scenery, bloom, external cast shadows, watermark or lettering. Detailed photographic creature materials under neutral diffuse lighting, with readable large forms rather than indiscriminate microtexture.",
    "editTargetSha256": "dbe050da48a5f4efecde87acbe18dbc8cc0ec453d77f1411ec7acdc91b9cb1c4",
    "styleReference": {
      "file": "tools/texture_sheets/sources/shambler-2026-10-01.png",
