    "refinementPrompt": "Make a precise correction to Image 1, the current menacing Armagon UV atlas. Image 2 is the prior atlas as a correspondence/reference for chest anatomy; Image 3 is the owner's enhanced Shambler as the facial menace/material reference.\n\nIMPORTANT DISCOVERY FROM THE ACTUAL MODEL:\nThe circular breathing grille near x200,y590 in this1323\u00d71189 atlas is a CHEST PORT, not the head. The giant fang ring around it stretches across the pectorals on the model. Correct this mapping rather than enlarging that ring.\n\n1. RESTORE THE CHEST: In the LEFT/front half around the circular breathing core (roughly x150..390,y410..810), remove the oversized ivory fangs and enclosing monster-mouth ring. Restore coherent heavy rib/tendon/scarred flesh and biomechanical connections around the original breathing core, using Image2 for correspondence. Keep the core at exactly its current position. It can be gruesome and powerful but must read as chest anatomy and machinery, not a second face. No long horizontal teeth across the chest.\n\n2. CREATE THE TRUE MENACING HEAD: The actual front HEAD maps to the small left-pointing region centred at x107,y591. Its broader skull/cheek area is x52..150,y493..720. Put the threatening skull-face HERE. Face upper brow/crown is toward smaller x (LEFT), lower jaw toward larger x (RIGHT); the two sides of the face are separated along image y. Do not rotate into an upright face. Use a heavy scarred brow, deeply recessed dark facial planes, a BLACK tooth-filled mouth and large irregular aged-ivory fangs fitted to this small head region, with convincing thick lip/gum folds. The Shambler is a guide to frightening facial character, not an anatomy donor. Make the head legible and predatory without expanding the mouth back across the chest.\n\nKeep all remaining flesh, back-half anatomy, cannon shapes/materials, waist connector, original palette families, all four flame islands, every outer UV-island silhouette/position and pure black background unchanged. Preserve exact1323\u00d71189 framing. Both body halves remain sideways, frontLEFT/backRIGHT; no new faces on the back, arms, guns or legs. Do not add external protrusions, new islands, captions, text, bloom or shadows. Maintain photographic creature quality and broad readable forms, not extra grain.",
