    "orientationPrompt": "Correct ONLY the small head/face area of Image 1. The chest and mechanical breathing port now map correctly; keep them unchanged.\n\nThe current small face is drawn as a LEFT-FACING PROFILE, which makes the mouth point upward when mapped onto the actual model. Replace it with a FULL FRONTAL FACE ROTATED 90 DEGREES COUNTERCLOCKWISE in the atlas. BOTH cheeks and BOTH eye sockets must be visible. This is NOT a side profile.\n\nThink of turning the entire atlas90degrees CLOCKWISE: the new face must then look UPRIGHT, DIRECTLY TOWARD THE VIEWER, with the eyes above the mouth.\n\nPrecise targets on the1324\u00d71188 image:\n- Work only within x52..150,y493..720 in the LEFT/front body half.\n- Two fierce, recessed eye sockets near (76,565) and (76,625): same x, separated along image y.\n- Heavy brow/crown toward x55..70.\n- Nose/central facial bridge near (94,595).\n- Dark gaping mouth centred near (116,595), long opening axis along IMAGE Y.\n- Upper fang row on the LEFT edge of that mouth, lower fang row on its RIGHT edge; the teeth point inward across IMAGE X.\n- Lower jaw toward x140.\nNo snout or open mouth protruding left beyond x52.\n\nMake this a vicious scarred biomechanical skull-face with irregular ivory fangs, deeply shadowed mouth and heavy angular brow, using Image2 (the owner's enhanced Shambler) for menace and flesh quality. Preserve the pale hide/dark wound palette. The chest breathing grille at roughly(200,590) remains a separate unchanged machine component, not another mouth.\n\nKeep absolutely everything outside the head/cheek edit area unchanged: both sideways body halves, back, all guns, muscle/tendon anatomy, waist, four flame islands, silhouettes, framing, resolution and black background. No text, new islands, extra faces, bloom or external shadows.",
    "orientationRefinement": "Rotate ONLY the small monster FACE on the extreme left middle of this texture atlas by 90 degrees COUNTERCLOCKWISE. It is currently upright, with two eyes above its mouth. That is WRONG for this sideways model UV. In the corrected texture the TWO EYES must be vertically stacked, both to the LEFT of the mouth. The forehead faces the LEFT edge; chin faces RIGHT toward the circular chest breathing grille. The mouth must be a WIDE HORIZONTAL gape along image Y after rotation, seen front-on. Preserve the same face, fangs, materials and menace, but turn its orientation. Fit the rotated face inside x40..155,y490..715, stretching to fit that region if necessary. Keep EVERY other pixel/content unchanged, including all chest anatomy, grille, cannons, flame islands, back half and black background. Do not rotate the entire atlas. Do not leave the eyes horizontally side-by-side above the mouth. No text.\n",
